# Health checks for the published services - one URL per line, `#` comments
# stripped before use. Checked on 127.0.0.1 rather than the tailscale IP on
# purpose: these answer "is the app answering", and a tailscale blip must not
# page 15 times at once - the published path itself is `tailscaled`, which is a
# runit unit sv-watch already watches.
#
# Any HTTP status counts as UP (302 and 401 are healthy here - half these
# services redirect to a login). Only `000`, meaning nothing answered at all,
# is a failure. Two consecutive strikes are required before a page, so a cold
# boot with containers still starting never alerts.
#
